    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n- [X] I have updated 'mini.nvim' to latest version\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.files\n\n### Description\n\nWhen inside a folder that contains a single entry, typing `o` results in the single entry to be removed (at least according to the UI).\n\n### Neovim version\n\nv0.10.0-dev-1425+gd2e7cc68e\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Create a new folder called `foo`, inside it create another folder called `bar`, and inside `bar` create `bar.txt`.\r\n2. Add the following configuration in `foo/config.lua`:\r\n```lua\r\nlocal install_path = vim.fn.fnamemodify('plugins/minifiles', ':p')\r\n\r\nif vim.fn.isdirectory(install_path) == 0 then\r\n  vim.fn.system({\r\n    'git',\r\n    'clone',\r\n    '--depth=1',\r\n    'https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.files',\r\n    install_path,\r\n  })\r\nend\r\nvim.opt.runtimepath:append(install_path)\r\n\r\nlocal minifiles = require('mini.files')\r\n\r\nminifiles.setup()\r\nvim.keymap.set('n', '<C-e>', function()\r\n  minifiles.open()\r\nend, {})\r\n```\r\n3. Inside `foo` run `nvim --clean -u config.lua`.\r\n4. Type `<C-e>` to open the `mini.files` explorer, go inside `foo`, and while the cursor is on `foo.txt` type `o`.\r\n\n\n### Expected behavior\n\n(Following my example above) For `foo.txt` to still be listed after pressing `o`.\n\n### Actual behavior\n\n`foo.txt` is gone.\r\n\r\n<img width=\"1135\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/assets/62502207/1a134b12-b78b-4796-a3c9-b6ec15fb5825\">\r\n",
