            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the issue!\r\n\r\nI can not reproduce this on `NVIM v0.10.0-dev-82b1a38` (latest Nightly). Neither with my usual config, nor with this repro. Judging by the version, it is built from source, right? Could you, please, check on latest Nightly build?\r\n\r\nThat said, there were recently some changes in core to how `o` works but I don't think they should matter here. The behavior described here is something that [explicitly dealt with](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/f699158e6a654d2778e446d98de2881d7ab1f5fb/lua/mini/files.lua#L1790-L1795).",
